    [
     1,
     "Dear All,<div>I would be very pleased if you could support me with the interpretation of the Scaling correction factor - Yuan-Bentler correction (Mplus Variant) - generated by the MLR estimator.</div><div>I have a p-value (Chi-square) equal to 0.182 and a scaling correction factor equal to 0.937. </div><div>I am not sure about the meaning of this last value and its interpretation.</div><div>Thank you so much.</div><div>Maria Sassi</div><div><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "SEyH6DkiDQAJ",
   "from": "Andy Supple",
   "author": "515b030b2cb5ea36",
   "date": "2020-07-28T16:13:56Z",
   "subject": "Re: MLR estimator",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The scaling correction as I understand it is telling you how much the Chi-square value was scaled due to nonnormality. If you multiply the MLR chi-square by the scaling factor, you will get the ML chi-square value. A .937 is quite small in terms of a scaling correction.<div><br></div><div>Andy</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Tue, Jul 28, 2020 at 10:47 AM Sassi Maria &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mars...@unipv.it</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Dear All,<div>I would be very pleased if you could support me with the interpretation of the Scaling correction factor - Yuan-Bentler correction (Mplus Variant) - generated by the MLR estimator.</div><div>I have a p-value (Chi-square) equal to 0.182 and a scaling correction factor equal to 0.937. </div><div>I am not sure about the meaning of this last value and its interpretation.</div><div>Thank you so much.</div><div>Maria Sassi</div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
